elaine: FYI -- AtlasEdge reserved pool signed (22k RPS equiv). Need an ops walk+priming run this week. Key asks: confirm autoscale thresholds, loadtest cadence, and a rollback play. Who's available?

hugo: I can take autoscale policy. Preference: conservative scale-down to avoid thrash; allow fast scale-up for bursts. What SLOs are we aiming for?

elaine: Target p95 <= 130ms for single-turn text gen, <= 180ms for multi-turn chat. Customer requests p4d for tail latency, but open to a100 for cost. Also want a short "cost window" test to estimate per-token $ at peak.

sam: I'll own loadtesting. Plan: shadow run first, then a 90m validation: smoke 20m, ramp 25m, soak 45m. I'll use a k6 harness that tags prompt-length buckets. Need an ephemeral token + traffic CSV.

nora: I'll author the runbook and the postmortem template. Include steps: prime KV (top-50 prefixes), model cache prime, verify fallback route to redwood-slim. Add circuit-breaker test to simulate 10% node loss.

ops-bot: Ephemeral credential requested by sam. Token-created: tok-77b4 (expires 03:45 hours). Audit entry: ae-1729.

hugo: Autoscale draft: triggers = [queue_len > 180, gpu_mem_pct > 80, p95_latency > 150ms sustained 25s]. Cooldowns: up=18s, down=150s. Min_replicas=8, max_replicas=48. Add emergency manual-scale webhook and an alert if fallback routing > 2% of requests. Also enforce per-GPU concurrent-stream soft cap = 28.

elaine: Add a graceful fallback route: if available capacity < 12%, route non-critical low-temp jobs to redwood-slim; tag those events. Also require backlog drain verification after scale-down.

sam: k6 snippet I'll use: ```js
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';
const lines = open('atlas_traffic.csv').split('\n');
export default function() {
  const body = {input: lines[Math.floor(Math.random()*lines.length)]};
  const res = http.post('https://api.redwood.example/v1/chat', JSON.stringify(body), {headers: {Authorization: `Bearer ${__ENV.TOKEN}`}});
  check(res, { 'status 200': r => r.status === 200 });
  sleep(0.01);
}
```

nora: Runbook items: prechecks (quota active, pool health, fallback warm), smoke, ramp, soak, failure injection (1 node OOM, 1 zone latency bump), post-checks (latency histogram, batching distrib, fallback ratio, billing estimate). Also include a customer-facing note about warmup billing and expected early tail cost.

hugo: For batching tuning: prefer tokens-per-batch target = 6 for median requests, allow up to 10 in steady state. Enable dynamic KV prefetch for top-100 prefixes. Also add an internal metric: tokens_per_batch 95pct should not exceed 14.

elaine: Proposed window: Thu 01:30-03:00 UTC (low traffic). Sam/Nora please confirm availability. I'll notify AtlasEdge account team and include the preflight checklist.

sam: Confirmed. I'll push k6 scripts + step-by-step runbook to the runbooks channel + link the metrics dashboard at least 2 hours before window.

nora: Confirmed. I'll also attach rollback play: immediate scale-to-min false, failover to redwood-slim, and contact list for escalation.

ops-bot: Run created: run-9901 scheduled 2025-09-18T01:30:00Z. Runbook doc id: rb-9901 (private).

elaine: Thanks all. Hugo please attach the final autoscale YAML in the PR, and Sam please include the billing estimate script. We'll do a short readiness call 30m before start.
